  "notes": "{摘|つ}む is a godan verb meaning to pluck or pick with the fingers.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を particle: 〜を{摘|つ}む\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{摘|つ}んでいる describes the ongoing action of picking.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {花|はな}を{摘|つ}む: to pick flowers\n- {茶|ちゃ}を{摘|つ}む: to pick tea leaves\n- {芽|め}を{摘|つ}む: to nip buds / nip in the bud (also figurative)\n- いちごを{摘|つ}む: to pick strawberries\n\nKANJI DISTINCTION (same reading):\n- {摘|つ}む: to pluck, pick\n- {積|つ}む: to pile up, stack\n- {詰|つ}む: to be stuck, checkmated",
